Coach App
*Updated 2026-10-12 to match the Harbor design. The design is the source of truth.*
*Since ADR-023 (2026-10-05) this is the rinkside page inside the coach website (/coach/rinkside), not a separate app.*
Seperate App from bladebook website. The app needs to be able for the coach to mark the student as checked in, no show, or can Cancel lesson.

Also needs to show the coach who has signed up for lessons that day and what time the lesson is at.

<!-- Also needs to be able to cancel the whole day, part of a day, the whole week, part of the week, and specific lessons all within a cancel section. 
    Note: the check in section also has a cancel functionality so a single lesson can be canceled in two places in the Coach app. -->


The checkin app will allow a coach to cancelan individual lesson, or any lessons ~~that day~~ *from today to the end of this week (the Week tab, see C_Rinkside Cancel Several Lessons.md)*. When canceling the coach will be asked if they want to release or hold the slots. 
    Hold: ~~means they are coach held~~ the time stays closed (a held lesson time) *(revised 2026-10-13, ADR-031)*
    Release: means they are rebookable by othr students
*Design:* cancelling one lesson is under the "..." button on its card, kept away from Present and No-show. It always
confirms, names the family who will be emailed, and asks Release for rebooking or Hold it closed (ADR-009 d5a).
A lesson that has started can't be cancelled, and cancelling needs signal.

*Design (today.html), the Today tab:*
  A progress bar: how many of today's lessons are recorded, and who's next.
  Each lesson card: time, skater, length. Present and No-show buttons once the lesson is within 10 minutes of starting;
  before that it shows "Starts at <time>". A recorded lesson shows Present or No-show with the time, and Undo straight after.
  A held slot shows "Held slot", closed to everyone.
  Tabs along the bottom: Today, Week, Account (see C_Rinkside Account.md).
  No signal: see C_Rinkside Offline.md.

The app needs to also have a sign in screen where the coach is validated that they are who they say they are. 
*Design (signin.html):* the same login email and password as the website (ADR-014 d10). The page says the app shows today's lessons, records attendance and cancels lessons; the schedule, students and payments stay on the website.


The app also needs to display the clients contact info at checkin
*Design:* tapping a skater's name shows the family's name, phone and email, each with a Copy button. Fetched with signal for that tap only and never stored on the phone (ADR-014 d9b). With no signal it says "Contact details need a connection."

